{"line": "header", "transcript": "11-hostile-artifact-references", "demonstrates": "Every way a Field can try to make core read or write somewhere it should not, and the digest lies it can tell. A traversal handle, an absolute path, a Windows device name, a staged file that is a symlink out of the staging directory, a digest that does not match the staged bytes, and a digest-only reference for bytes the notebook does not have.", "gate": "a2-normative", "operation": "collect", "mode": "incremental", "expected_outcome": "failed", "expected_exit_code": 10, "notes": "Each case is shown once for review; in the conformance kit each is its own run, because the first violation fails the run. Note that no Field-supplied string is ever a path component: the handle grammar is a single segment from a closed character set, and the notebook path is derived only from core's own digest."}
